  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two ways into provideGlance()",
      "items": [
        "Broken by design: the platform re-bind sends APPWIDGET_UPDATE, Glance 1.1.1 runs the whole composition inside the receiver's goAsync window on a cold-starting process, the scope is cancelled and runAndLogExceptions discards the CancellationException silently (M0 findings 6).",
        "Warm, onUpdate to provideGlance measured 1.6 s; that is the budget the cold start has to fit.",
        "Fixed: BOOT_COMPLETED to enqueueUniqueWork to a CoroutineWorker with its own execution window, then updateAll().",
        "A/B in one session: control (receiver disabled) never left the placeholder; 4 of 4 treatments rendered, 26-36 s after boot_completed.",
        "The fix is not a first-frame guarantee: 3 of 4 treatments drew a complete first frame. In run 3 the Chronometer ticked with no ring, and one refresh fixed it; dumpsys showed the full 240x240 bitmap was already in the RemoteViews, so the omission was on the host's side."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Who is allowed to call whom",
      "items": [
        "onUpdate has exactly one production caller: the platform. APPWIDGET_UPDATE is a protected broadcast, so neither adb nor a normal app may send it.",
        "Our code never talks to the launcher: Glance calls updateAppWidget(), and AppWidgetService hands the RemoteViews to the AppWidgetHost that renders them.",
        "Every internal widget signal is an explicit intent; implicit custom-action broadcasts do not reach manifest receivers on API 26+.",
        "updatePeriodMillis=0 means nothing retries a missed frame, so the periodic self-heal is load-bearing, not belt-and-braces."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Measured platform limits (M0)",
      "items": [
        "canScheduleExactAlarms() is false on the test device; setExactAndAllowWhileIdle() throws SecurityException. USE_EXACT_ALARM is reserved for alarm-clock and calendar apps.",
        "Inexact setAndAllowWhileIdle arrived +90 s late in light Doze, and was deferred rather than lost when the device stayed idle.",
        "The ring is a static frame; only the text ticks. The Chronometer base is elapsedRealtime(), which resets on reboot, so it must be recomputed on every render and never persisted.",
        "Measurements went to files/m0_render_log.txt in app-private storage because logcat lost the decisive line."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Probe code, not the target architecture",
      "items": [
        "Throwaway, delete before M2: SpikeRingWidget, SpikeRing.kt, SpikeRefreshReceiver, SpikeProbeReceiver, BootRefreshReceiver, RefreshWidgetsWorker.",
        "The boot fix lives in :widget only because Glance is on :widget's classpath; in M2 the refresh policy moves to :core:scheduler behind an interface (T2.12/T2.13) and the direct updateAll() call is replaced there.",
        "Included but still scaffolding: :core:model, :core:time, :core:mortality, :core:data, :core:scheduler, :feature:config (settings.gradle.kts). They hold no runtime role in this trace."
      ]
    }
  ]
